#HELPS
1 ACROBAT~
Acrobats are a polite euphemism for agile burglars and second-story men. These
thieves avoid detection by stealth, and rely on mobility and cunning to avoid
capture.

Positive attributes: Agility, Endurance
Negative attributes: Intelligence

Hp per level: 1d6

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Acrobatics, Athletics
Can train up to 75%: Marksman, Sneak
Can train up to 50%: Unarmored, Speechcraft, Alteration
Can train up to 25%: Spear, Hand to hand, Light armor
~
1 AGENT~
Agents are common operatives skilled in deception and avoidance,  also trained
in self-defense and the use of deadly force. Self-reliant and independent, the
agents devote themselves to personal goals, or to various patrons or causes.

Positive attributes: Personality, Agility
Negative attributes: Strength

Hp per level: 1d6

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Speechcraft, Sneak
Can train up to 75%: Acrobatics, Light armor
Can train up to 50%: Short blade, Mercantile, Conjuration
Can train up to 25%: Block, Unarmored, Illusion
~
1 ARCHER~
Archers are fighters specializing in long-range combat and rapid movement. They
keep their opponents at distance by ranged weapons, swift maneuver, and engaged
in melee with sword and shield after the enemy is wounded and weary.

Positive attributes: Agility, Strength
Negative attributes: Endurance

Hp per level: 1d8

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Marksman, Long blade
Can train up to 75%: Block, Athletics
Can train up to 50%: Light armor, Unarmored, Spear
Can train up to 25%: Restoration, Sneak, Medium armor
~
1 ASSASSIN~
Assassins are killers who rely on stealth and mobility to approach the victims
undetected. Execution with ranged weapons or with short blades for close work.
Assassins include ruthless murderers and principled agents of noble causes.

Positive attributes: Agility, Intelligence
Negative attributes: Charisma

Hp per level: 1d6

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Sneak, Marksman
Can train up to 75%: Light armor, Short blade
Can train up to 50%: Acrobatics, Security, Long blade
Can train up to 25%: Alchemy, Block, Athletics
~
1 BARBARIAN~
Barbarians are the proud, savage warrior elite of the plains nomads, mountain
tribes, and sea reavers. They tend to be brutal and direct, lacking civilized
graces, but they glory in heroic feats, and excel in fierce, frenzied single
combat.

Positive attributes: Strength, Agility
Negative attributes: Intelligence

Hp per level: 1d8

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Axe, Medium armor
Can train up to 75%: Blunt weapon, Athletics
Can train up to 50%: Block, Acrobatics, Light armor
Can train up to 25%: Armorer, Marksman, Unarmored
~
1 BARD~
Bards are loremasters and storytellers. They crave adventure for the wisdom and
insight to be gained, and must depend on weapons, shield, spell and enchantment
to preserve them from the perils of their educational experiences.

Positive attributes: Personality, Intelligence
Negative attributes: Strength

Hp per level: 1d6

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Speechcraft, Alchemy
Can train up to 75%: Acrobatics, Long blade
Can train up to 50%: Block, Mercantile, Illusion
Can train up to 25%: Medium armor, Enchant, Security
~
1 BATTLEMAGE~
Battlemages are combat-wizards, trained in both lethal spellcasting and heavily
armored combat. They sacrifice their mobility and versatility for the ability
to supplement melee and ranged attacks with elemental damage.

Positive attributes: Intelligence, Strength
Negative attributes: Endurance

Hp per level: 1d4

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Alteration, Destruction
Can train up to 75%: Conjuration, Axe
Can train up to 50%: Heavy armor, Mysticism, Long blade
Can train up to 25%: Marksman, Enchant, Alchemy
~
1 HEALER~
Healers are spellcasters who swear solemn oaths to heal the afflicted and cure
the diseased. When threatened, they defend with reason, disabling attacks and
magic, relying on deadly force only in extremity.

Positive attributes: Willpower, Personality
Negative attributes: Strength

Hp per level: 1d4

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Restoration, Mysticism
Can train up to 75%: Alteration, Hand to hand
Can train up to 50%: Speechcraft, Illusion, Alchemy
Can train up to 25%: Unarmored, Light armor, Blunt weapon
~
1 KNIGHT~
Knights of noble birth, distinguished in battle or tourney, are high civilized
warriors, schooled in letters and courtesy, governed by the codes of chivalry.
In addition to the arts of war, many knights also study the lore of healing and
enchantment.

Positive attributes: Strength, Personality
Negative attributes: Intelligence

Hp per level: 1d8

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Long blade, Axe
Can train up to 75%: Speechcraft, Heavy armor
Can train up to 50%: Block, Restoration, Mercantile
Can train up to 25%: Medium armor, Enchant, Armorer
~
1 MAGE~
Mages claim to study magic for its intellectual rewards, but they often profit
from its practical applications. Varying widely in temperament and motivation,
mages share but one thing in common, the avid love of spellcasting.

Positive attributes: Intelligence, Willpower
Negative attributes: Strength

Hp per level: 1d4

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Mysticism, Destruction
Can train up to 75%: Alteration, Illusion
Can train up to 50%: Restoration, Enchant, Alchemy
Can train up to 25%: Unarmored, Short blade, Conjuration
~
1 MONK~
Monks are the students of the ancient martial arts of hand-to-hand combat and
unarmored self defense. They often avoid detection by high stealth, mobility,
and agility, and are skilled with a variety of ranged and close-combat weapons.

Positive attributes: Agility, Willpower
Negative attributes: Intelligence

Hp per level: 1d6

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Hand to hand, Unarmored
Can train up to 75%: Athletics, Acrobatics
Can train up to 50%: Sneak, Block, Marksman
Can train up to 25%: Light armor, Restoration, Blunt weapon
~
1 NIGHTBLADE~
Nightblades are nibble spellcasters who use their magics to enhance mobility,
concealment, and stealthy close combat. They have a sinister reputation, since
many nightblades are thieves, enforcers, assassins, or covert agents.

Positive attributes: Willpower, Agility
Negative attributes: Personality

Hp per level: 1d4

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Mysticism, Illusion
Can train up to 75%: Alteration, Sneak
Can train up to 50%: Short blade, Light armor, Unarmored
Can train up to 25%: Destruction, Marksman, Security
~
1 PILGRIM~
Pilgrims are travellers and seekers of truth and enlightenment. They fortify
themselves for road and wilderness with arms, armor, and magic, and through
wide experience of the world, they become shrewd in commerce and persuasion.

Positive attributes: Personality, Endurance
Negative attributes: Strength

Hp per level: 1d6

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Speechcraft, Mercantile
Can train up to 75%: Marksman, Restoration
Can train up to 50%: Medium armor, Illusion, Hand to hand
Can train up to 25%: Short blade, Block, Alchemy
~
1 ROGUE~
Rogues are adventurers and opportunists with a gift for getting in and out of
trouble. Relying variously on charm and dash, blades and business sense, they
thrive on conflict and misfortune, trusting to luck and cunning to survive.

Positive attributes: Agility, Personality
Negative attributes: Willpower

Hp per level: 1d8

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Short blade, Mercantile
Can train up to 75%: Axe, Light armor
Can train up to 50%: Hand to hand, Block, Medium armor
Can train up to 25%: Speechcraft, Athletics, Long blade
~
1 SORCERER~
Sorcerer though spellcasters by vocation, they rely mostly on summonings and
enchantments. They are greedy for magic scrolls, rings, armor and weapons, and
commanding undead and Daedric servants gratifies their egos.

Positive attributes: Intelligence, Endurance
Negative attributes: Agility

Hp per level: 1d4

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Enchant, Conjuration
Can train up to 75%: Mysticism, Destruction
Can train up to 50%: Alteration, Illusion, Medium armor
Can train up to 25%: Heavy armor, Marksman, Short blade
~
1 SPELLSWORD~
Spellswords are spellcasting specialists trained to support Imperial troops in
skirmish and in battle. The veteran spellswords are prized as mercenaries, and
well-suited for careers as adventurers and soldiers-of-fortune.

Positive attributes: Willpower, Endurance
Negative attributes: Strength

Hp per level: 1d4

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Block, Restoration
Can train up to 75%: Long blade, Destruction
Can train up to 50%: Alteration, Blunt weapon, Enchant
Can train up to 25%: Alchemy, Medium armor, Axe
~
1 THIEF~
Thieves are pickpockets and pilferers. Unlike the robbers, who kill and loot,
thieves typically choose stealth and subterfuge over violence, and they often
entertain romantic notions with charm and cleverness.

Positive attributes: Agility, Intelligence
Negative attributes: Willpower

Hp per level: 1d6

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Security, Sneak
Can train up to 75%: Acrobatics, Light armor
Can train up to 50%: Short blade, Marksman, Speechcraft
Can train up to 25%: Hand to hand, Mercantile, Athletics
~
1 WARRIOR~
Warriors are the professional men-at-arms, soldiers, mercenaries, and common
adventurers of the Empire, trained with various weapons and armor styles,
conditioned by long marches, and hardened by ambush, skirmish, and battle.

Positive attributes: Strength, Endurance
Negative attributes: Intelligence

Hp per level: 1d8

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Long blade, Medium armor
Can train up to 75%: Heavy armor, Athletics
Can train up to 50%: Block, Armorer, Spear
Can train up to 25%: Marksman, Axe, Blunt weapon
~
1 PRIEST~
Priest are specialists trained mostly in the ways of restoration. They claim to
study magic for its common cause, but they often profit from its benefits. Like
mages they share the avid love of spellcasting.

Positive attributes: Willpower, Personality
Negative attributes: Endurance

Hp per level: 1d4

Proffecions:
Can train up to 99%: Restoration, Mysticism
Can train up to 75%: Alteration, Blunt weapon
Can train up to 50%: Unarmored, Conjuration, Speechcraft
Can train up to 25%: Light armor, Alchemy, Destruction
~
1 BLOCK~
The Block proficiency allows the hero to use shields to block one melee attack.
Shields will not protect you from ranged and magical attacks.

Actions: Block, Bash

Skills: Disarm, Taunt

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Block action will make you avoid a enemy's attack. You have to equip a shield
in order to use this skill.

Check to succeed: Skill % /10 + dexterity.
Cost: 10.
~
1 ARMORER~
The Armorer profficiency is used to maintain weapons and armor items at top
effectiveness.  Damaged weapons do less damage. Damaged armor provides less
protection against  attacks. As wear increases, the diminishing effectiveness
of weapons and armor  becomes dramatic.

Acions: Execute, Gouge, Pummel, Overpower

Skills:  Hammer, Sharpen, Reinforce
~
1 SECURITY~
The Security proficiency lets you open locked doors and containers with thief
tools like lockpicks, disarm traps with probes, and re-seal sealed documents
after reading them.

Actions: Distract

Skills: Lockpick, Track, Scan, Detrap
~
1 SNEAK~
The Sneak proficiency is the art of moving unseen and unheard. Skilled sneaks
are also adept pickpockets. Sneak is a very useful skill, as it allows for
critical hits.

Actions: Fade, Disengage

Skills: Pickpocket, Sneak, Hide, Backstab

Sneak skill will allow you to walk silently and creature will not see you.

Skill to succeed: Skill % /2 + intelligence.
Duration: 12 turns.
Cost: 10
~
1 ENCHANT~
Enchant proficiency is the process of permanently applying a magical effect to
an item  by harnessing the power of a creature's soul. This skill governs the
creation, use, and recharging of enchanted items.

Actions: Blink, Banish

Skills: Scribe, Meditate, Enchant, Imbue

Enchant skill will allow you to enchant armor and clothing with a positive
effect. You will need a runestone to do this.

Check to succeed: Skill % /2 + intelligence.
Cost: 10.
~
1 ALCHEMY~
Alchemy proficiency allows you to identify magical properties in ingredients
and create potions to generate useful effects, such as healing, cure disease,
water-walking, magical shielding, and fortifying bodily attributes.

Actions: None

Skills: Brew, Cook, Poison, Aid
~
1 HEAVY_ARMOR~
The Heavy Armor proficiency is used to move and defend while wearing massive
and rigid armors like iron, steel, silver, Dwemer, ebony, and Daedric armor.

Actions: None

Skills: Heavy armor

As higher you train these armor skills, the more armor you will receive from
wearing armor of this category.

About skill:
The heavy armor skill will allow you to wear all armor items flaged as heavy
armor style.
~
1 MEDIUM_ARMOR~
The Medium Armor proficiency lets one move and defend while wearing durable but
flexible armors like chain, scale, bonemold, and Orcish armor.

Actions: None

Skills: Medium armor

As higher you train these armor skills, the more armor you will receive from
wearing armor of this category.

About skill:
The medium armor skill will allow you to wear all armor items flaged as medium
armor style.
~
1 LIGHT_ARMOR~
The Light Armor profiency lets one move and defend while wearing light-weight,
flexible armors like leather, boiled leather, fur, chitin, and glass.

Actions: None

Skills: Light armor

As higher you train these armor skills, the more armor you will receive from
wearing armor of this category.

About skill:
The light armor skill will allow you to wear all armor items flaged as light
armor style.
~
1 HAND_TO_HAND~
The Hand-to-hand skill is the martial art of unarmed combat.

Actions: Slam, Kick, Punch, Grip

Skills: Cestus

As higher you train these weapon skills, the more damage you will deal with the
weapons of this category.~
1 LONG_BLADE~
The Long Blade proficincy lets the hero use broadswords, sabers, longswords,
claymores, katanas, and dai-katanas effectively.

Actions: None

Skills: Claymore, Longsword, Broadsword

As higher you train these weapon skills, the more damage you will deal with the
weapons of this category.
~
1 BLUNT_WEAPON~
The Blunt Weapon proficiency makes you more effective when using heavy bashing
weapons like maces, hammers, clubs, or staves.

Actions: None

Skills: Mace, Warhammer, Staff

As higher you train these weapon skills, the more damage you will deal with the
weapons of this category.
~
1 AXE~
he Axe skill helps a user wield heavy chopping weapons like war axes and
battleaxes more effectively.

Actions: None

Skills: Battleaxe, Waraxe

As higher you train these weapon skills, the more damage you will deal with the
weapons of this category.
~
1 MARKSMAN~
The Marksman profficiency affects the use of ranged weapons such as the short
bow, long bow, crossbow, dart, throwing star, and throwing knife.

Actions: None

Skills: Archery (Bows, Throwing weapons, Crossbows)

As higher you train these weapon skills, the more damage you will deal with the
weapons of this category.
~
1 SHORT_BLADE~
Short Blade proficiency makes hero be more effective with short, quick, weapons
like daggers, tantos, short swords, and wakizashis.

Actions: None

Skills: Dagger, Shortsword

As higher you train these weapon skills, the more damage you will deal with the
weapons of this category.

~
1 SPEAR~
The Spear proficiency permits effective use of long-hafted thrusting weapons
like spears and halberds.

Actions: None

Skills: Spear, Halberd

As higher you train these weapon skills, the more damage you will deal with the
weapons of this category.
~
1 DESTRUCTION~
The Destruction proficiency is the mastery of the spell effects of the College
of Destruction. Their spells harm living and unliving things, like elemental
damage, draining, damaging, vulnerability, and disintegration magical effects.

Actions: None

Skills:
Shock damage, Frost damage, Fire damage, Poison damage, Drain attribute
Drain fatigue, Drain magicka, Drain health, Damage attribute, Damage fatigue,
Damage magicka, Damage health, Weakness to element, Disindegrade weapon and
armor.
~
1 ALTERATION~
Thhe Alteration proficiency manipulates the physical world and its natural
properties. Alteration effects include water breathing and walking, jumping,
levitating, burdening, opening and locking, and creating shield barriers
against physical and elemental damage.

Actions: None

Skills: Burden, Feather, Levitate, Shield, Elemental shield

~
1 ILLUSION~
The Illusion profficiency includes spells that alter the perceptions and
thoughts of living beings. Illusion effects include blindness, illumination,
paralysis, silence, calmness, enragement, charm, distract, camouflage, and
invisibility.

Actions: None

Skills:
Blindness, Chameleon, Charm, Demoralize, Frenzy, Invisibility, Paralysis,
Sanctuary, Sound
~
1 CONJURATION~
The Conjuration proficiency include the mental domination of mundane and
magical creatures, summoning of otherworldly weapons and armor, and summoning
of Daedric or undead servants and powers to serve and protect the caster.

Actions: None

Skills: Summon scamp, Bound weapons and armor
~
1 MYSTICISM~
The Mysticism proficiency shapes and focus otherworldly forces to bind souls in
gems, teleport the caster's body, manipulate the world with telekinesis, absorb
or reflect magical energies, and sense unseen objects at a distance.

Actions: None

Skills:
Absorb attributes, Absorb fatigue, Absorb magicka, Absorb Health
~
1 RESTORATION~
The Restoration proficiency heals, restores, and fortify the body's attributes
and abilities, cure disease, and protect it from other malign influences.

Actions: None

Skills:
Fortify attributes, Fortify health, Fortify fatigue, Fortify magicka, Restore
attributes, Restore health, Restore magicka, Restore Fatigue, Restistance to
elements, Immunity to elements.
~
1 ATHLETICS~
The Athletics proficiency trains and conditions one for running and swimming.

Actions: Enrage, Grapple, Dodge

Skills: Dig, Rescue, Charge
~
1 ACROBATICS~
The Acrobatics skill involves jumping, climbing, and avoiding damage from
falls.

Actions: Tumble, Pounce

Skills: Climb, Mount
~
1 SPEECHCRAFT~
The Speechcraft proficiency allows hero to influence others. Listeners are more
willing to divulge information or to entrust tasks to the skilled speaker.

Actions: None

Skills: Intimidate, Bluff, Judge
~
1 MERCANTILE~
The Mercantile proficiency is the art of buying low and selling high. This
skill guarantees lower initial prices for goods, equipment, and services, and
improves chances of getting better deals by bargaining.

Actions: None

Skills: Bandage, Peek, Inspect
~
1 BANDAGE~
This skill can be use to restore yours or other's health by 1-12 points.

Chance to succced: Skill % /2 + willpower
Cost: 10.
~
1 PEEK~
This skill is automatic skill that will allow the hero to get a fast look into
the victim's inventory.
~
1 INSPECT~
This skill will allow you to inspect an weapon's or armor's statistics like the
damage, armor, weight and value.

Chance to succeed: Skill % /2 + personality.
Cost: 10.
~
1 INTIMIDATE~
This skill will allow you to intimidate a victim and make it give you and item
it equips. If unsuccessful your favor will go down by 10 points.

Chance to succeed: Skill % /2 + personality - victim's level.
Cost: 10.
~
1 BLUFF~
This skill will allow you to make an npc give you info about itself like its
health, magicka, fatigue, ac and thac0.

Chance to succeed: Skill % /2 + personality.
Cost: 10.
~
1 JUDGE~
This skill will allow you to know the alignment of the victim. Especially when
you dont want to kill good npcs.

Chance to succeed: Skill % /2 + personality.
Cost: 10.
~
1 CLIMB~
This skill will allow you to pass through exits that require climbing.
~
1 MOUNT~
This skill will allow you to mount creature without falling.
~
1 CHARGE~
This skill will allow you o charge against an enemy and get a mighty hit.

Chance to succeed: Skill % /2 + strength.
Effect: 1d12 + strength /2.
Cost: 10.
~
1 ENRAGE~
This automatic action will allow you to be enraged in combat, adding extra
damage to your attacks.

Chance to succeed: Skill % /10 + willpower.
Effect: Strength /2 points.
Duration: Luck /2 turns.
Cost: 10.
~
1 GRAPPLE~
This automatic action will allow you to grapple with the enemy receiving +2
agility and substracting -2 agility from the enemy.

Chance to succeed: Skill % /10 + endurance
Effect: +2 / -2 agility.
Duration: Endurance /2.
Cost: 10.
~
1 DODGE~
This automatic action will avoid an incomming attack from enemy.

Chance to succeed: Skill % /10 + agility.
Cost: 10.
~
1 DISEASE_IMMUNITY~
This spell will allow your target to gain immunity from disease.
If immune the damage dealt will be zero.

Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + duration /2.
~
1 PARALYSIS_IMMUNITY~
This spell will allow your target to gain immunity from pralysis.
If immune the damaged dealt will be zero.

Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + duration /2.
~
1 POISON_IMMUNITY~
This spell will allow your target to gain immunity from poison attacks.
If immune the damaged dealt will be zero.

Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + duration /2.
~
1 FORTIFY_STRENGTH~
This spell will allow you to increase target's strength for a period.

Effect: 1-2.
Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + effect + duration /2.
~
1 FORTIFY_ENDURANCE~
This spell will allow you to increase target's endurance for a period.

Effect: 1-2.
Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + effect + duration /2.
~
1 FORTIFY_AGILITY~
This spell will allow you to increase target's agility for a period.

Effect: 1-2.
Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + effect + duration /2.
~
1 FORTIFY_INTELLIGENCE~
This spell will allow you to increase target's intelligence for a period.

Effect: 1-2.
Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + effect + duration /2.
~
1 FORTIFY_WILLPOWER~
This spell will allow you to increase target's willpower for a period.

Effect: 1-2.
Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + effect + duration /2.
~
1 FORTIFY_PERSONALITY~
This spell will allow you to increase target's personality for a period.

Effect: 1-2.
Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + effect + duration /2.
~
1 FORTIFY_LUCK~
This spell will allow you to increase target's luck for a period.

Effect: 1-2.
Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + effect + duration /2.
~
1 FORTIFY_ATTACK~
This spell will allow you to increase target's hitroll for a period.

Effect: 1-5.
Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + effect + duration /2.
~
1 FORTIFY_FATIGUE~
This spell will allow you to increase your current fatigue.

Effect: Current fatigue * 2.
Cost: 10 + effect + effect /2.
~
1 FORTIFY_HEALTH~
This spell will allow you to increase your current health.

Effect: Current health * 2.
Cost: 10 + effect + effect /2.
~
1 FORTIFY_MAGICKA~
This spell will allow you to increase your current magicka.

Effect: Current magicka * 2.
Cost: 10 + effect + effect /2.
~
1 DISEASE RESISTANCE~
This spell will allow your target to gain resistance to disease. If resistant
you will dealt less damage from this kind of spells.

Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + duration /2.
~
1 POISON_RESISTANCE~
This spell will allow your target to gain resistance to poison. If resistant
you will dealt less damage from this kind of spells.

Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + duration /2.
~
1 FROST_RESISTANCE~
This spell will allow your target to gain resistance to frost. If resistant you
will dealt less damage from this kind of spells.

Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + duration /2.
~
1 FIRE_RESISTANCE~
This spell will allow your target to gain resistance to fire. If resistant you
will dealt less damage from this kind of spells.

Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + duration /2.
~
1 SHOCK_RESISTANCE~
This spell will allow your target to gain resistance to shock. If resistant you
will dealt less damage from this kind of spells.

Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + duration /2.
~
1 MAGIC_RESISTANCE~
This spell will allow your target to gain resistance to magic. If resistant you
will dealt less damage from this kind of spells.

Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + duration /2.
~
1 PARALYSIS_RESISTANCE~
This spell will allow your target to gain resistance to paralysis. If resistant
you will dealt less damage from this kind of spells.

Duration: 1d60 + willpower.
Cost: 10 + duration /2.
~
1 RESTORE_STRENGTH~
This spell will allow you to restore your target's strength even if it is
permanently damaged.

Effect: 2.
Cost: 10 + effect.
~
1 RESTORE_ENDURANCE~
This spell will allow you to restore your target's endurance even if it is
permanently damaged.

Effect: 2.
Cost: 10 + effect.
~
1 RESTORE_AGILITY~
This spell will allow you to restore your target's agility even if it is
permanently damaged.

Effect: 2.
Cost: 10 + effect.
~
1 RESTORE_INTELLIGENCE~
This spell will allow you to restore your target's intelligence even if it is
permanently damaged.

Effect: 2.
Cost: 10 + effect.
~
1 RESTORE_WILLPOWER~
This spell will allow you to restore your target's willpower even if it is
permanently damaged.

Effect: 2.
Cost: 10 + effect.
~
1 RESTORE_PERSONALITY~
This spell will allow you to restore your target's personality even if it is
permanently damaged.

Effect: 2.
Cost: 10 + effect.
~
1 RESTORE_LUCK~
This spell will allow you to restore your target's luck even if it is
permanently damaged.

Effect: 2.
Cost: 10 + effect.
~
1 RESTORE_HEALTH~
